  Placement: 0
  CardStory: 'The first few hours were worse. The moment the thread was severed from
    that holy spool, and enjoined with the stuff my soul is made of. What glorious
    pain, to have scales ripped from my eyes and actually see for the first time
    in my life.

    

    But pain is pain, no matter how honored. Sensation magnified
    a thousandfold, insight sharpened so thin that I cut myself with every thought.
    No, not cut. I am ripped apart from my own mind, each feeling and memory crystal
    clear and all the more dangerous for it.

    

    I revel in it now. I can
    feel down to the last infinitesimal part of it. How the blackened string creeps
    across my skin and within it, burrowing and wiggling, an extension and a parasite
    and a blessing. Through the devotion we ascend, and now I must prove mine.'
